title: The Gates Are Locked
subtitle: Employers lock out their workers.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('lockout'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('lockout');
Q.lw_n = RG.lw.rnd(4, 22);
RG.news('Lockout at ' + Q.lw_works.replace(/^the /, '') + ': ' + Q.lw_n + ',000 shut out', 2);
!}

= The Gates Are Locked

On Monday morning the workers of **[+ lw_works +]** found the gates chained and a notice on them: the works will reopen for those who sign a new contract, with longer hours and without the works council. [+ lw_n +] thousand men and women stand in the street in [+ lw_town +]. [? if year >= 1922 : With the mark falling every week, a month without wages is a famine. ?]

- @occupy: Climb the gates and occupy the works.
- @kitchens: Open soup kitchens and hold out.
- @arbitrate: Take it to the state arbitrator.

@occupy
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] [? if lw_d_mil >= 50 : The district is angry enough to hold it. ?][? if lw_d_mil < 50 : The security police may clear it in days. ?]
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids occupations.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('councils');
if (Math.random() < 0.3 + Q.lw_d_mil / 200) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: 7, members: 0.06, loyalty: 5});
    RG.news('Workers occupy ' + Q.lw_works.replace(/^the /, ''), 2);
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {repression: 12, members: -0.04});
}
if (Q.ultraleft_gone) { RG.lw.lean('offensive', 2, 5); } else { RG.lw.lean('ultraleft', 1, 4); }
!}

[? if lw_out = 1 : The red flag goes up over the boiler house at dawn. After nine days the employers reopen on the old contract. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : On the fourth day the security police come in armoured cars, and the occupiers leave with their hands on their heads. ?]

@kitchens
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The families eat, and the workforce holds together.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: 8, members: 0.04});
!}

The soup kitchens open in the union hall and two church halls. After six weeks the workers go back on a compromise, and nobody signs the new contract.

@arbitrate
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A quick compromise, and calmer streets.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids working through the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('union_work');
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {militancy: -6});
Q.spd_relation += 3;
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 5);
!}

The arbitrator splits the difference: an hour more a week, and the works council stays. The gates open after twelve days.
